WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Tap any word in the mushaf, and its meaning appears above, card by card.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:23.636
Drag across the cards to follow a phrase, or step through it word by word.

00:00:23.636 --> 00:00:36.818
On a keyboard, the arrow keys move between words, and Shift selects a phrase.

00:00:36.818 --> 00:00:55.844
Select ٱلْفَلَقِ and ask about the full range of its root.

00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:09.344
ف ل ق means to split something open. It appears in just four places in the Quran.

00:01:09.344 --> 00:01:23.844
Seeds and fruit stones split open in Al-Anʿām 6:95, and the reader follows the link.

00:01:23.844 --> 00:01:59.901
The same root describes the sea parting for Musa in Ash-Shuʿarāʾ 26:63.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:12.287
So we ask how the sea fits the same idea.

00:02:12.287 --> 00:03:04.787
Seed, night and sea: each time, something closed splits open, and what it hid comes out.

00:03:04.787 --> 00:03:09.037
Read. Select. Ask. Discover.
